## Native functions that take a C function pointer (ImplementationPlan.md
## 5.10.10 'Native callbacks', 5.10.14; M15.a item 5 'Callbacks'). Native
## code that calls an '<msil>fn_' address enters managed code without a
## reverse-P/Invoke transition, so until P3-B's thunks every live call or
## address reference that native lookup binds to a name of the callback list
## (a sorted table behind lld::msil::isNativeCallbackFunction: qsort,
## pthread_create, _beginthreadex, CreateThread, lfind, _lfind, signal, ...)
## is the link error
##   native function '<name>' (<module>) takes a C function pointer;
##   passing functions to native code needs phase 3 thunks
## with '>>> referenced by' lines, after LTO. It holds:
## - for qsort from an ELF shared object, also when the call passes no
##   function (signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_IGN));
## - for pthread_create from a MinGW import library, _beginthreadex and
##   CreateThread from MSVC import libraries;
## - for lfind through oldnames' alias to _lfind (both names are listed);
## - for each of the 46 names of the list on its own (the section 12 rows of
##   2026-10-22 and 2026-10-23 for 5.10.10 and 5.10.14: the 36 names of
##   5.10.14 and glibc's other spellings __sysv_signal, bsd_signal, ftw64,
##   nftw64, scandir64, scandirat, scandirat64, sigset, ssignal and
##   sysv_signal), from an ELF shared object on x86_64 Linux and from an
##   import library on windows-msvc: one error per name, each naming the
##   symbol that the bitcode calls, and no P/Invoke (so lfind and _lfind are
##   each proven, which the alias case alone cannot tell apart);
## - for an address-only reference;
## - for a declaration that import_name alone binds to qsort.
## The text names the symbol that the bitcode references, never the import
## entry (the section 12 row of 2026-10-22 for 5.10.14): 'my_sort' for the
## import_name declaration, 'lfind' for the alias.
## No error for an explicit import_module qsort (explicit imports are the
## workaround), for a listed name that bitcode defines, or for a listed
## declaration that no code references after LTO.

